      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8838456::page::004",
        "PMC8838456::page::007"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The hcp phase has a higher superconducting transition temperature than the bcc phase.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sc addition enhances superconductivity through formation of the hcp phase.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sc-Hf-Nb-Ta-Ti-Zr alloys will exhibit enhanced superconductivity relative to Hf-Nb-Ta-Ti-Zr parent alloys.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Superconducting properties of the Hf-Nb-Ta-Ti-Zr parent alloys have been reported in the literature and can serve as a baseline.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The alloys are synthesized by arc melting under an Ar atmosphere.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "X-ray diffraction, scanning electron microscopy, and energy-dispersive X-ray spectroscopy are used to characterize the alloys.",
      "field": "conditions",
